 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
 
+## Board publication
+
+Only account admins (including the owner) with access to a board can publish or unpublish it. Publication does not change board membership or grant edit access.
+
+- `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication` publishes the board. Returns `201 Created` with the board JSON and its secret `public_url`. Publishing an already-published board keeps the same URL.
+- `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication` unpublishes it. Returns `204 No Content`. Its `public_url` is now `null`; publishing again generates a new URL.
+
+Anyone with the link can open these read-only HTML pages without signing in:
+
+- `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key`
+- `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Only published cards are visible. Unpublishing the board revokes all three kinds of links.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
diff --git a/test/integration/public_boards_test.rb b/test/integration/public_boards_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4679f06
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/integration/public_boards_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class PublicBoardsTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
+  setup do
+    @board = boards(:writebook)
+    @card = cards(:logo)
+    @column = @card.column
+  end
+
+  test "the board JSON includes a stable URL until the board is unpublished" do
+    sign_in_as :kevin
+    assert_nil board_json.fetch("public_url")
+
+    post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_response :created
+    public_url = response.parsed_body.fetch("public_url")
+    assert_equal public_board_url(@board.reload.publication), public_url
+    assert_equal public_url, board_json.fetch("public_url")
+
+    post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_equal public_url, response.parsed_body.fetch("public_url")
+
+    delete board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_response :no_content
+    assert_nil board_json.fetch("public_url")
+
+    post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_not_equal public_url, response.parsed_body.fetch("public_url")
+    sign_out
+
+    [ public_url, "#{public_url}/columns/#{@column.id}", "#{public_url}/cards/#{@card.number}" ].each do |url|
+      get url
+      assert_response :not_found
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "anonymous visitors can navigate from board to column to published card" do
